*VRAM-resident Vulkan prover pipeline (`qsag-accel`).* A zero-`crates.io`-dependency Linux Vulkan 1.3 / SPIR-V 1.5 backend executes *10 compute shaders*: six standalone primitive kernels (Keccak-f[1600], Poseidon2-12, Goldilocks NTT, Ext2 coset LDE, Poseidon2 Merkle layers, and BDOZ binary-field dot products) plus *four VRAM-resident WHIR/Hem prover shaders* (`air_row_group_a.comp`, `air_row_group_b.comp`, `whir_lde_merkle.comp`, `whir_fold_sumcheck.comp`) managed through persistent `ProverArena` / `GpuWhirSession` slots (`ProverKernelSlot`) with `32 MiB` chunked host staging. The Poseidon2 shaders (`poseidon2_perm12.comp`, `merkle_layer_poseidon2.comp`, and the two AIR row shaders) implement the canonical profile of §3.2, and the GPU WHIR session supports up to 24 variables. `vulkan_ffi.rs` supports discrete GPUs and unified-memory `VK_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_TYPE_INTEGRATED_GPU` APUs, enforcing Wave32 / zero-scratch pipeline audits and keyed `cSHAKE256` V5 `ExecutionReceipt` computation reports on the six primitive shader slots (not hardware remote attestation; the four prover-stage shaders do not yet issue receipts).

= Four assurance pillars

Across the `208` modules registered in `Qsag.lean` and `AuditAxioms.lean`, organized into specification, mathematics, coding, oracle, protocol, custody, execution, machine, and top-level directories, a cold warnings-as-errors build followed by our constructive kernel audit (`withEnv (env.setExporting false) Lean.collectAxioms`) verifies *`96,449` public and `.olean.private` declarations (`48,484` theorems)* with *`0` `sorry`, `0` custom axioms, and `0 Classical.choice`*—permitting solely `{propext, Quot.sound}` via `PSum` extractors and structural `BEq` lemmas. In `aeneas/lean`, the MIR/spec/custody closure audits `6,546` MIR + `132` spec-weld + `89` custody-weld declarations (`0` rejected axioms, `0 FunsExternal`), paired with the `aeneas/lean-whir` WHIR closure. Sandboxed six-kernel comparator replay (`lean`, `leanchecker-paranoid`, `lean4lean`, `nanoda_bin`, `con-leche`, `con-ron`) covers *`130` `Qsag.Apex` theorems*, *`71` MIR challenge theorems*, and *`57` WHIR MIR challenge theorems*. Hardened `#verify_inhabited` (preventing unbound `List` witnesses from collapsing to empty `default` lists) and `#tooth_pair` (`AssuranceKit.lean`) guard theorem premises across the spine (@pillars).

