== GPU primitive shaders and `ProverArena` end-to-end WHIR proving

On an *AMD Radeon RX 6750 XT (RDNA 2)* (Vulkan 1.3.289, RADV 24.2.8, Wave32, zero scratch, raw-log SHA-256 `9b128cfa...4fe8`), one warmed transfer-inclusive audit run verified bit-exact parity and V5 `ExecutionReceipt`s across all six primitive shaders against `CpuReferenceBackend` (@gpubench; buffer-scrubbed reruns measured `21.35 ms` Poseidon2-12 and `35.38 ms` Merkle), while `VK_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_TYPE_INTEGRATED_GPU` enumerates unified-memory APUs (`AMD Radeon 890M`). End-to-end `ProverArena` execution across the four VRAM-resident WHIR shaders (`air_row_group_{a,b}`, `whir_lde_merkle`, `whir_fold_sumcheck`) with `cpu_fallbacks = 0` and bit-exact CPU proof SHA3-256 parity achieves *`321.7 ms` direct* and *`597.0 ms` with outer commitment-chain + 16-bit fold PoW* on a 32-signer Beam subnet ($n_v = 22$, `16.77M` codeword) versus `1.56–1.59 s` on 24-thread CPU (`2.62×–4.95×` faster; verify p50 `5.75 ms`), while `32 MiB` chunked staging cuts peak host RSS *`15.8×` from `9.47 GiB` to `613.3 MiB`* (`687.9 / 841.1 ms` on mixed Jorts+Corduroy, verify `7.64 ms`). On a full 128-signer shard ($n_v = 24$, `67.11M` codeword), the current tree proves in *`1.56–1.57 s`* with Vulkan NTTs and row evaluation while the Canopy and opening work stays on the CPU, against `3.67–3.73 s` on 22 CPU workers; the exact line-evaluator rewrite of §4.5 cut the CPU row sumcheck from `754 ms` to `524–538 ms`. An earlier fully VRAM-resident `ProverArena` run recorded `1.13–1.34 s` direct (`743–766 MiB` host RSS vs. `9.0–9.8 GiB` CPU); that figure has not been re-measured on the current tree. Contiguous GPU allocations remain bounded by RADV's `4 GiB` `maxStorageBufferRange` (so an unsharded 1,200-signer `4.83 GB` WHIR buffer falls back to CPU unless sharded).

